// XFAIL: RT-M2-9: a type of 2^61 bytes or more, `[u64; 1usize << 61]`, has its size computed modulo 2^64 (0): `size_of` prints 0 and a local of it gets no room in the frame while its indexing allows 2^61 elements; it builds at -O0 and -O2; rustc refuses the type (too big for the current architecture) (0.30.2)
// From the g302frame review (its open part of RT-M2-9). Since v0.30.1
// at least (it prints 0 and exits 0 at both levels). The fix, 6986b630d
// and its case tests/run/rt_m2_009_type_size_wraps.vl, is on s301std,
// g302std and g302stack2, none of them merged into release-0.30.2: this
// is that case's program on the release, to be removed when the fix
// merges with its own case. Its error there is the one below (g302std's
// build, first at the size_of).
// ERROR: values of the type '[u64; 2305843009213693952]' are too big for the target
// ERROR: rt_m2_009r_type_size_wraps.vl: line 13, column 19
fn main() {
    let n = std::env::args().count();
    println("{}", std::mem::size_of::<[u64; 1usize << 61]>());
    if n > 5 {
        let mut a = [0u64; 1usize << 61];
        for i in 0..(64 * n) {
            a[i] = 0xDEAD;
        }
        println("{}", a[3]);
    }
}
